{
  "id": "u02-l04",
  "unit": "u02-pronouns",
  "title": "Is, isn't & yes/no",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "To ask a yes/no question, add **কি** (*ki*), usually right after the subject: **আপনি কি শিক্ষক?** 'Are you a teacher?' Spelling: **কি** (short ি) is the question marker; **কী** (long ী) means 'what'. They sound the same: **এটা কী?** 'What is this?' vs **ওটা কি আম?** 'Is that a mango?'\n\n'Is' has no word in Bengali, but **'is not'** does, and it changes with the person:\n\n- আমি ছাত্র **নই**: I'm not a student\n- তুমি ছাত্র **নও**: you're not\n- আপনি / উনি ছাত্র **নন**: you / he (polite) aren't\n- সে / এটা **নয়**: he / it isn't\n\n**নয় or নেই?** **নয়** (and নই / নও / নন) denies *what* someone is: রাফি ডাক্তার **নয়**. **নেই** denies that someone is *there*: রাফি এখানে **নেই**.\n\n**এটা / ওটা** = this / that. **কে** = who.",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "ki-q",
      "bn": "কি",
      "tr": "ki",
      "en": "(yes/no question marker)",
      "notes": "Turns a statement into a yes/no question: আপনি কি শিক্ষক? Usually comes right after the subject. Short ি — compare কী 'what'."
    },
    {
      "id": "noi",
      "bn": "নই",
      "tr": "noi",
      "en": "am not",
      "notes": "Goes with আমি / আমরা: আমি ছাত্র নই."
    },
    {
      "id": "noo",
      "bn": "নও",
      "tr": "noo",
      "en": "are not (familiar)",
      "notes": "Goes with তুমি / তোমরা."
    },
    {
      "id": "non",
      "bn": "নন",
      "tr": "non",
      "en": "is not / are not (polite)",
      "notes": "Goes with আপনি, তিনি, উনি."
    },
    {
      "id": "noy-isnt",
      "bn": "নয়",
      "tr": "noy",
      "en": "is not",
      "notes": "Goes with সে, ও, এটা. In everyday Bangladeshi speech না is used for all persons: আমি ছাত্র না. নয় is also the number nine (Unit 5)."
    },
    {
      "id": "ke",
      "bn": "কে",
      "tr": "ke",
      "en": "who"
    },
    {
      "id": "eta",
      "bn": "এটা",
      "tr": "eta",
      "en": "this",
      "notes": "এ 'this' + classifier -টা. Spoken BD also এইটা (eita)."
    },
    {
      "id": "ota",
      "bn": "ওটা",
      "tr": "ota",
      "en": "that",
      "notes": "ও 'that' + classifier -টা. Spoken BD also ওইটা (oita)."
    }
  ],
